[[9792,3735,"There was extensive BWV footage in this case, which both I and the jury were able to see multiple times. It appeared to me, (and presumably to the jury, given their conclusion), that the officers at the scene were trying to take Neal's welfare into account. The real issue was around their training. Whilst there may not have been any realistic or practicable alternative to restraining Neal, at least initially, it was clear from the evidence that none of the officers recalled their training which","prolonged restraint",""],[9793,3735,"The training gives no guidance as to what constitutes","undefined prolonged restraint",""],[9794,3735,"One of the witnesses questioned whether the guidelines applied at all if somebody is under arrest, particularly regarding","guideline applicability uncertainty",""],[9795,3735,"The College of Policing slides regarding ABD state that a","incorrect category 1 expectation",""],[9796,3735,"The guidelines also refer to providing","misunderstanding of chemical sedation",""],[9797,3735,"Is there a better way for the College of Policing to ensure that the training has worked and is embedded?","training effectiveness verification",""]]